    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Baxter Real Estate are delighted to bring to the market this attractive two-bedroom mid-terrace family home, extending to approximately 60 sq. m / 646 sq. ft.\n\nThe accommodation briefly comprises an entrance hallway leading to a bright and spacious living room, featuring laminate flooring, an open fireplace and a large window providing plenty of natural light.\n\nTo the rear of the property is a kitchen/dining area with tile-effect vinyl flooring and a tiled splashback. A back door provides access to a south-west-facing, low maintenance rear garden, offering an ideal space for outdoor dining and relaxation.\n\nAt first-floor level, there are two bedrooms and a fully tiled family bathroom with a bath. \n\nAn additional benefit is the floored attic space, complete with a skylight and Stira staircase, providing excellent additional storage. The attic also offers potential for future conversion, subject to the necessary planning permission and compliance with relevant building regulations.\n\nThe property further benefits from off-street parking to the front, double-glazed uPVC windows and gas-fired central heating, with the gas boiler having been recently upgraded. \n\nSituated in a quiet cul-de-sac, this home enjoys a convenient location close to a wide range of local amenities, including primary and secondary schools, shops and public transport links. Blanchardstown Shopping Centre is also within easy reach.\n\nThe property enjoys excellent access to both the N3 and M50 motorway, providing convenient connections to Dublin City Centre and the wider national road network.\n\nThis property is likely to appeal to first-time buyers, downsizers and investors alike, and early viewing is highly recommended.\nPlease note: All descriptions, dimensions, references to condition, and necessary permissions for use and occupation, together with all other details, are provided in good faith and are believed to be correct. However, intending purchasers should not rely on them as statements or representations of fact and should satisfy themselves by inspection or otherwise as to the accuracy of each item. No appliances have been tested, and purchasers should carry out their own investigations regarding the condition of all appliances and any other information provided."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Living Room - 5m (16'5\") x 8.83m (29'0\")\nOpen fire place, laminate flooring and a large wndow\n\nKitchen/Dining Room - 3.83m (12'7\") x 2.62m (8'7\")\nTile-effect vinyl flooring, tiled splashback, and doors leading to south-west facing garden\n\nBedroom 1 - 3.87m (12'8\") x 3.78m (12'5\")\nLaminate flooring\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.85m (12'8\") x 2.38m (7'10\")\nLaminate flooring\n\nBathroom - 2.59m (8'6\") x 1.42m (4'8\")\nTiled walls and floor, a bath with an electric shower\n\nNotice\nPlease note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate and photographs provided for guidance only."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> 2 bedroom/ 1 bathroom mid-terrace family home </li><li> Double Glazed uPVC windows and Gas Central Heating System (upgraded boiler) </li><li> South-West facing, low maintenance rear garden and driveway to front </li><li> Floored attic with a skylight and stira ladder </li><li> Situated on a quiet cul-de-sac with access to large green area </li><li> All local amenities within walking distance </li><li> Frequent and direct public transport to Dublin City Centre </li><li> Short walking distance to Blanchardstown Shopping Centre </li><li> Short drive distance to the N3 and M50</li></ul>"
      },
